SoundCraft VAIO preview

Unofficial SoundCraft adaptation for Ubuntu Xenial i386 on the Sony VAIO P.
Based on SoundCraft 0.12.1, e85a4801e9029c9a1f5ce536b11be65aea832ed8.
Not an official ArtCraft build. Original notices and contributor credits remain.

The application and CLI keep the upstream engine, audio formats, DSP, MIDI,
session editing and plugin-host code. The desktop uses Glow/OpenGL on this
machine's software renderer. Initial preferences use a 1500 x 650 window and
4096-frame audio buffer; later saved user choices are retained. VAIO cursor
blinking/animations are disabled and live meters refresh at 12 Hz. Idle windows
redraw on events; autosave writes and error notifications remain active. Existing
system fonts are read at runtime, not redistributed; egui font notices are included.

Commands: soundcraft-vaio and soundcraft-vaio-cli. The normal APT frontend owns
installation, updates and removal. No self-updater or background login service.
The private libxcb is application-local; system libraries are unchanged.

SoundCraft is pre-alpha. Work on copies and keep original media. Headless
editing, mixing, session save/reopen, FLAC/WAV and resampling have acceptance
checks; the output-only fixture verifies native CPAL/ALSA playback separately.
Third-party plugins require matching Linux i386 builds and may be expensive or
unstable. No arbitrary plugin compatibility or incumbent-DAW parity is promised.
Recording, external interfaces, MIDI hardware, suspend/resume and large-session
capacity require separate verification. This port never upgrades the operating
system or enables microphone capture during automated playback checks.

Source/recipes and exact build hashes are in build.json and the corresponding
source archive. Audio repair uses the existing snd_hda_intel position_fix=1
configuration; this package does not install or change an audio driver.
